// Title: Use of TTDInject.exe
// Sigma ID: b27077d6-23e6-45d2-81a0-e2b356eea5fd
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-05-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects the executiob of TTDInject.exe, which is used by Windows 10 v1809 and newer to debug
//   time travel (underlying call of tttracer.exe)
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Ttdinject/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_ttdinject.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "ttdinject.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "TTDInject.EXE"
